### 3. Proje Tanıtım Metni (Space Apps & GitHub `README.md` Şablonu)

Yarışma teslim sayfasında ve GitHub deponuzda doğrudan kullanabileceğiniz kısa ve teknik tanıtım metni:

> **SPHEREx Time-Series Sky Explorer (Planet X & SPHEREx)**
> **Overview:**
> This tool queries NASA/IPAC IRSA's SPHEREx archive (`spherex.obscore`) to generate chronological near-infrared time-lapse animations (GIFs) for any given celestial object name or ICRS coordinate (`RA`/`Dec`). By aligning multi-epoch cutouts within consistent spectral bands ($0.75 - 5.0\ \mu\text{m}$), the tool enables rapid visual detection of high-proper-motion objects (brown dwarfs, asteroids, comets, Planet X candidates) and variable stars.
> **Key Features:**
> * **Flexible Target Resolution:** Accepts object names (resolved via SIMBAD/CDS) as well as sexagesimal (`HMS/DMS`) or decimal degree coordinates.
> * **Automated Epoch Deduplication & Sampling:** Groups dithered exposures by observation date, filters out partial edge frames via WCS footprint verification, and selects evenly spaced chronological epochs.
> * **Astronomical Image Pipeline:** Performs real-time `Cutout2D` extraction and `ZScale + Asinh` intensity stretching on Multi-Extension FITS (MEF) data using parallel worker threads.
> * **Verified Test Targets:** Validated on Barnard's Star, Epsilon Indi B, WISE 0855, RW Aurigae, and R Draconis.
> 
